    "body": "Add seventeen shared laws supporting a bounded search for an indexed pair whose actual elliptic-curve sum passes one quadratic-character gate. The report gives a hand procedure that computes every row parity from two univariate product/remainder trees, preserves repeated records and keys, and derives miss probability at most2^(-t) after t independent column-record masks. Executable search and measured performance remain separate work. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe algebra is generic in its shared owner: finite binary-mask counts, repeated-root Taylor coefficients and forbidden nonzero-factor correction, then the actual Weierstrass carry identity. Prime-field point-addition and indexed-product assemblies apply these laws unchanged. Claim PCC-20261116-67338a has thirteen attestation subjects and unverified standing. [pcc:unverified]\n\nValidation: canonical gate002 audits236 theorems with0 failing and0 trusted-native exceptions; all17 named compiler axiom prints use only allowed standard axioms. All three final PDF pages were rendered and inspected. Failed gate001 and every focused failed source/log are retained. No proof limits, inventory, trust or linter policies changed; no fresh independent checker or hosted pass is asserted. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPreservation: all50 old subjects and13 new subjects match their hashes; the original seven-row PCC ledger is an exact byte/parsed prefix of eight rows. Source/prose whitespace check exits0; archival diff-check exits2 on preserved raw diagnostic spaces. PR22 closing autonomy/outcome and receipts accompany this substantive change. Consumer conflicts/closing records remain separate. [pcc:unverified]\n\nSee docs/character-parity-20261116.md, its prospective proof map, and docs/character-parity-20261116/PUBLICATION.md plus the inspected three-page PDF. Simultaneous-gate conjunction, implicit-family extraction and useful original-relation yield remain open. The original complete ECDLP algorithm criterion remains unmet. No new numerical/native case, paid or qualification execution was performed. [pcc:unverified]\n\nLanded at2026-11-16T05:14:35Z as02ea8d8b86a611eb92048a8cfd01cea701163623, retaining published head911c04bd11a166a2232ba339eec42a282e6db98b. Same-head hosted run43808916444 failed: jobs133105952984 and133105953246 each have zero steps, with explicit annotations that the account is locked due to a billing issue. This is not a hosted pass; no retry or payment was performed. All63 landed claim subjects match their pinned bytes, the published eight-row ledger is byte-identical at merge, and the original seven-row byte/parsed prefix is retained. [pcc:unverified]\n",
